    "chunk_text": "w\u00e6\u00f0 to Aarone: Ga ongean Moyses on \u00fe\u00e6t westen; & he for ongean hine to Godes dune & & Moyses rehte Aarone ealle Drihtnes word \u00fee he hine fore sende, & \u00fea tacn \u00fee he hym bebead. & hi foron \u00e6tg\u00e6dere & gegaderodon ealle \u00fea yldestan of Israhela m\u00e6g\u00fee. & Aaron sp\u00e6c ealle \u00fea word \u00fee God spr\u00e6c to Moyse, & worhte tacn beforan eallum \u00feam folce. & \u00fe\u00e6t folc gelyfde & hi gehyrdon \u00fe\u00e6t Drihten gemiltsode Israhela m\u00e6g\u00f0e & \u00fe\u00e6t he geseah heora \u00c6FTER \u00feison Moyses & Aaron eodon in & cw\u00e6don to Pharaone: Ebrea God het secgan \u00fee \u00feas \u00feing, & he andwyrde, & cw\u00e6\u00f0: Hw\u00e6t is se Drihten, \u00fe\u00e6t ic him hyran scule & Israhela folc forl\u00e6tan; ne can \u00d0a cw\u00e6don hi: Ebrea God us bebead \u00fe\u00e6t we foron \u00fereora daga f\u00e6reld on \u00fe\u00e6t westen, \u00fe\u00e6t we offrian \u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Farao, Egypta cyng, to Moyse & to Aarone: Hwi myrra\u00f0 gyt \u00feis folc fram heora weorcum; & Farao cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his folce: Ge geseo\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feis Ebreisce folc is micel & wyxt swy\u00f0e & swy\u00feor wile, gyf Witodlice Pharao bebead on \u00f0am d\u00e6ge \u00feam weorcgerefum & \u00fe\u00e6s folces \u00feenum, \u00feus cwe\u00feende: Ne & asetta\u00fe him \u00fe\u00e6t illce tigolgeweorc \u00fee hi \u00e6r worhton, ne ge nan \u00feing ne gewanion; so\u00felice hy synd Beon hi gehynede & gef",
